    {
      "question": "At what point can you no longer contribute to a Roth IRA?",
      "type": "ai_overview",
      "text_blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "snippet": "You can no longer contribute to a Roth IRA when your modified adjusted gross income (MAGI) exceeds certain limits, which vary based on your filing status. For single filers, the limit is $165,000 in 2025, and for married couples filing jointly, it's $246,000. There is no age limit for contributing to a Roth IRA, as long as your income allows.",
          "reference_indexes": [
            0,
            1,
            3
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "snippet": "Income Limits for Roth IRA Contributions in 2025:",
